  {
    description: Requires to use \`"""\` or \`"\` for adding a GraphQL description instead of \`#\`.
Allows to use hashtag for comments, as long as it's not attached to an AST definition.,
    name: no-hashtag-description,
    recommended: true,
    schema: null,
    url: https://the-guild.dev/graphql/eslint/rules/no-hashtag-description,
  },
  {
    description: Disallow using root types \`mutation\` and/or \`subscription\`.,
    name: no-root-type,
    recommended: false,
    schema: {
      items: {
        additionalProperties: false,
        properties: {
          disallow: {
            items: {
              enum: [
                mutation,
                subscription,
              ],
            },
            minItems: 1,
            type: array,
            uniqueItems: true,
          },
        },
        required: [
          disallow,
        ],
        type: object,
      },
      maxItems: 1,
      minItems: 1,
      type: array,
    },
    url: https://the-guild.dev/graphql/eslint/rules/no-root-type,
  },
  {
    description: Avoid scalar result type on mutation type to make sure to return a valid state.,
    name: no-scalar-result-type-on-mutation,
    recommended: false,
    schema: null,
    url: https://the-guild.dev/graphql/eslint/rules/no-scalar-result-type-on-mutation,
  },
  {
    description: Enforces users to avoid using the type name in a field name while defining your schema.,
    name: no-typename-prefix,
    recommended: true,
    schema: null,
    url: https://the-guild.dev/graphql/eslint/rules/no-typename-prefix,
  },
  {
    description: Requires all types to be reachable at some level by root level fields.,
    name: no-unreachable-types,
    recommended: true,
    schema: null,
    url: https://the-guild.dev/graphql/eslint/rules/no-unreachable-types,
  },
  {
    description: Set of rules to follow Relay specification for Arguments.

- A field that returns a Connection type must include forward pagination arguments (\`first\` and \`after\`), backward pagination arguments (\`last\` and \`before\`), or both

Forward pagination arguments

- \`first\` takes a non-negative integer
- \`after\` takes the Cursor type

Backward pagination arguments

- \`last\` takes a non-negative integer
- \`before\` takes the Cursor type,
    name: relay-arguments,
    recommended: false,
    schema: {
      items: {
        additionalProperties: false,
        minProperties: 1,
        properties: {
          includeBoth: {
            default: true,
            description: Enforce including both forward and backward pagination arguments,
            type: boolean,
          },
        },
        type: object,
      },
      maxItems: 1,
      type: array,
    },
    url: https://the-guild.dev/graphql/eslint/rules/relay-arguments,
  },
  {
    description: Set of rules to follow Relay specification for Connection types.

- Any type whose name ends in "Connection" is considered by spec to be a \`Connection type\`
- Connection type must be an Object type
- Connection type must contain a field \`edges\` that return a list type that wraps an edge type
- Connection type must contain a field \`pageInfo\` that return a non-null \`PageInfo\` Object type,
    name: relay-connection-types,
    recommended: false,
    schema: null,
    url: https://the-guild.dev/graphql/eslint/rules/relay-connection-types,
  },
  {
    description: Set of rules to follow Relay specification for Edge types.

- A type that is returned in list form by a connection type's \`edges\` field is considered by this spec to be an Edge type
- Edge type must be an Object type
- Edge type must contain a field \`node\` that return either Scalar, Enum, Object, Interface, Union, or a non-null wrapper around one of those types. Notably, this field cannot return a list
- Edge type must contain a field \`cursor\` that return either String, Scalar, or a non-null wrapper around one of those types
- Edge type name must end in "Edge" _(optional)_
- Edge type's field \`node\` must implement \`Node\` interface _(optional)_
- A list type should only wrap an edge type _(optional)_,
    name: relay-edge-types,
    recommended: false,
    schema: {
      items: {
        additionalProperties: false,
        minProperties: 1,
        properties: {
          listTypeCanWrapOnlyEdgeType: {
            default: true,
            description: A list type should only wrap an edge type.,
            type: boolean,
          },
          shouldImplementNode: {
            default: true,
            description: Edge type's field \`node\` must implement \`Node\` interface.,
            type: boolean,
          },
          withEdgeSuffix: {
            default: true,
            description: Edge type name must end in "Edge".,
            type: boolean,
          },
        },
        type: object,
      },
      maxItems: 1,
      type: array,
    },
    url: https://the-guild.dev/graphql/eslint/rules/relay-edge-types,
  },
  {
    description: Set of rules to follow Relay specification for \`PageInfo\` object.

- \`PageInfo\` must be an Object type
- \`PageInfo\` must contain fields \`hasPreviousPage\` and \`hasNextPage\`, that return non-null Boolean
- \`PageInfo\` must contain fields \`startCursor\` and \`endCursor\`, that return either String or Scalar, which can be null if there are no results,
    name: relay-page-info,
    recommended: false,
    schema: null,
    url: https://the-guild.dev/graphql/eslint/rules/relay-page-info,
  },
  {
    description: Require deletion date on \`@deprecated\` directive. Suggest removing deprecated things after deprecated date.,
    name: require-deprecation-date,
    recommended: false,
    schema: {
      items: {
        additionalProperties: false,
        properties: {
          argumentName: {
            type: string,
          },
        },
        type: object,
      },
      maxItems: 1,
      type: array,
    },
    url: https://the-guild.dev/graphql/eslint/rules/require-deprecation-date,
  },
